hadiths[270]{hadithnumber,text}:
"205","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 205 Arabic Hadees: 2051"
"206","On the authority of Jabir ibn Sulaym (or Salim), who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and found him sitting with his companions. I said, ""Which of you is the Prophet (peace be upon him)?"" He said: Either he gestured to himself, or the people gestured to him. He said: And there he was, wearing a cloak (burdah) with its hem falling on his feet. I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, I am ignorant about many things, so teach me."" He said: ""Fear Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and do not belittle any good deed, even if it is pouring from your bucket into the vessel of one who asks for water. And beware of arrogance, for Allah, Blessed and Exalted, does not love arrogance. And if a man insults you and reproaches you with something he knows about you, do not reproach him with something you know about him; then you will have its reward and he will bear its sin. And do not insult anyone."""
"207","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 207 Arabic Hadees: 3044"
"208","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 208 Arabic Hadees: 3477"
"209","On the authority of Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, which people are most beloved to Allah? And which deeds are most beloved to Allah?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The most beloved of people to Allah the Exalted is the one who is most beneficial to people. And the most beloved of deeds to Allah the Mighty and Majestic is bringing joy to a Muslim, or relieving him of a distress, or paying off his debt, or dispelling his hunger. And for me to walk with a brother in regard to a need is more beloved to me than secluding myself in this mosque—meaning the Mosque of Medina—for a month. And whoever restrains his anger, Allah will cover his faults. And whoever suppresses his rage, even though he could act upon it if he wished, Allah will fill his heart with hope on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever walks with his brother regarding a need until it is fulfilled for him, Allah will make his footing firm on the Day when feet will slip. (And indeed, bad character spoils deeds just as vinegar spoils honey)."""
