"240","Abu Burdah narrated: I entered upon Abu Musa in the house of the daughter of Umm al-Fadl. I sneezed and he did not say ""Yarhamuk Allah"" (may Allah have mercy on you) to me. Then she sneezed and he said ""Yarhamuk Allah"" to her. So I returned to my mother and informed her. When she came to him, she said: ""My son sneezed in your presence and you did not say 'Yarhamuk Allah' to him, but she sneezed and you said 'Yarhamuk Allah' to her."" He said: ""Your son sneezed and did not praise Allah the Exalted, so I did not say 'Yarhamuk Allah' to him. But she sneezed and praised Allah the Exalted, so I said 'Yarhamuk Allah' to her. And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: 'When one of you sneezes and praises Allah, then say ""Yarhamuk Allah"" to him. And if he does not praise Allah the Mighty and Majestic, then do not say ""Yarhamuk Allah"" to him.'"" She said: ""You did well, you did well."""
