"258","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 258 Arabic Hadees: 2625"
"259","On the authority of ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: When we departed from Mecca, the daughter of Ḥamza followed us, calling out, ""O uncle! O uncle!"" I took her by the hand and brought her to Fāṭima (may Allah be pleased with her), saying, ""Here is your cousin's daughter.""When we arrived in Medina, I, Zayd, and Jaʿfar disputed over her. I said: ""I took her, and she is my cousin's daughter."" Zayd said: ""She is my brother's daughter."" Jaʿfar said: ""She is my cousin's daughter, and her maternal aunt is with me.""The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to Jaʿfar: ""You resemble me in creation and character."" He said to Zayd: ""You are our brother and our freed slave."" He said to me: ""You are from me and I am from you."" Then he said: ""Give her to her maternal aunt, for the maternal aunt is like a mother.""I said: ""Will you not marry her, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""She is my brother's daughter through breastfeeding."""
"260","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 260 Arabic Hadees: 2249"
"261","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 261 Arabic Hadees: 3020"
"262","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 262 Arabic Hadees: 3155"
"263","On the authority of Abdullah ibn Abbas, who said: Salman al-Farisi narrated his story to me from his own mouth. He said: I was a Persian man from the people of Isfahan, from a village thereof called Jayy. My father was the chief (Dihqan) of his village, and I was the dearest of Allah's creation to him. His love for me did not cease until he confined me in his house, like a slave-girl is confined, tending the fire. I strove hard in the Magian religion until I became the custodian of the fire, kindling it and never allowing it to go out for a single hour.

He said: My father had a large estate. One day he was busy with a building project, so he said to me: ""O my son! I am occupied with this building today regarding my estate, so go and inspect it."" He commanded me concerning it with some of what he wanted. I went out intending his estate, but I passed by a church of the Christians. I heard their voices therein as they were praying. I did not know the condition of people due to my father confining me in his house. When I passed by them and heard their voices, I entered upon them to see what they were doing.

He said: When I saw them, their prayer amazed me and I became inclined to their affair. I said: ""By Allah, this is better than the religion we are upon."" By Allah, I did not leave them until the sun set, and I neglected my father's estate and did not go to it. I said to them: ""Where is the origin of this religion?"" They said: ""In al-Sham (Syria).""

He said: Then I returned to my father, and he had sent people in search of me, and I had distracted him from all his work. When I came to him, he said: ""O my son! Where were you? Did I not entrust you with what I entrusted?"" I said: ""O my father! I passed by some people praying in a church of theirs, and what I saw of their religion amazed me. By Allah, I did not cease being with them until the sun set."" He said: ""O my son! There is no good in that religion. Your religion and the religion of your forefathers is better than it."" I said: ""Nay, by Allah, it is better than our religion.""

He feared for me, so he put fetters on my feet and confined me in his house. I sent word to the Christians, saying: ""When a caravan from al-Sham, Christian merchants, arrives, inform me of them."" A caravan of Christian merchants from al-Sham arrived. They informed me of them. I said to them: ""When they finish their business and intend to return to their land, notify me."" When they intended to return, they informed me. I threw off the iron from my feet and went out with them until I arrived in al-Sham.

When I arrived, I said: ""Who is the best of the people of this religion?"" They said: ""The bishop in the church."" I went to him and said: ""I have desired this religion and loved to be with you, serving you in your church, learning from you, and praying with you."" He said: ""Enter."" So I entered with him.

He was an evil man. He commanded them to give charity and encouraged them in it, but when they brought things to him, he hoarded them for himself and did not give them to the poor, until he had amassed seven jars of gold and silver. I hated him intensely for what I saw him doing. Then he died. The Christians gathered to bury him. I said to them: ""This was an evil man. He commanded you to give charity and encouraged you in it, but when you brought it to him, he hoarded it for himself and gave nothing of it to the poor."" They said: ""What is your knowledge of that?"" I said: ""I will show you his hoard."" They said: ""Show us."" I showed them its location. They brought out seven jars filled with gold and silver. When they saw them, they said: ""By Allah, we will never bury him."" So they crucified him and then stoned him. Then they brought another man and put him in his place.

Salman says: I never saw a man who did not pray the five prayers whom I consider better than him; more ascetic in the world, more desirous of the Hereafter, or more constant in worship night and day than him. I loved him with a love I had not loved anyone before him. I stayed with him for a time. Then death approached him. I said to him: ""O so-and-so! I was with you and loved you with a love I had not loved anyone before you. The decree of Allah has come upon you as you see. To whom do you commend me? And what do you command me?"" He said: ""O my son! By Allah, I know no one today upon what I was upon. The people have perished, altered, and abandoned most of what they were upon, except a man in 'al-Raml' (perhaps referring to a specific location or the wilderness), and he is so-and-so. He is upon what I was upon, so join him.""

When he died and was buried, I went to the man of al-Mawsil. I said to him: ""So-and-so commended me to you at his death and informed me that you are upon his affair."" He said to me: ""Stay with me."" So I stayed with him. I found him to be the best man upon the affair of his companion. He did not live long before he died. When death approached him, I said to him: ""O so-and-so! So-and-so commended me to you and commanded me to join you. The decree of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has come upon you as you see. To whom do you commend me? And what do you command me?"" He said: ""O my son! By Allah, I know no man upon the like of what we were upon except a man in Nisibis, and he is so-and-so. Join him.""

When he died and was buried, I went to the man of Nisibis. I came to him and informed him of my story and what my companion had commanded me. He said: ""Stay with me."" So I stayed with him. I found him upon the affair of his two companions. I stayed with the best of men. By Allah, he did not live long before death descended upon him. When he was attended, I said to him: ""O so-and-so! So-and-so commended me to so-and-so, then so-and-so commended me to so-and-so, then so-and-so commended me to you. To whom do you commend me? And what do you command me?"" He said: ""O my son! By Allah, we know no one remaining upon our affair whom I command you to come to, except a man in Ammuriyah (Amorium). He is upon the like of what we are upon. If you wish, go to him, for he is upon our affair.""

When he died and was buried, I went to the man of Ammuriyah and informed him of my story. He said: ""Stay with me."" So I stayed with a man upon the guidance of his companions and their affair. I acquired wealth until I had cows and sheep. Then the decree of Allah descended upon him. When he was attended, I said to him: ""O so-and-so! I was with so-and-so, then so-and-so commended me to so-and-so, and so-and-so commended me to so-and-so, then so-and-so commended me to you. To whom do you commend me? And what do you command me?"" He said: ""O my son! I know no one who has arisen upon what we were upon among the people whom I command you to come to. But the time of a Prophet has overshadowed you. He is sent with the religion of Ibrahim. He will emerge in the land of the Arabs, migrating to a land between two lava tracts (harrahs), between which are date palms. He has signs that are not hidden: he eats the gift but does not eat charity, and between his shoulders is the Seal of Prophethood. If you can reach that land, then do so.""

Then he died and was buried. I stayed in Ammuriyah as long as Allah willed. Then a group of Kalb merchants passed by me. I said to them: ""Will you carry me to the land of the Arabs? I will give you these cows and sheep of mine."" They said: ""Yes."" I gave them to them, and they carried me. When they brought me to Wadi al-Qura, they wronged me and sold me to a Jewish man as a slave. I was with him, and I saw the date palms. I hoped that this was the land my companion had described to me, but I was not certain in myself.

While I was with him, a cousin of his from Medina, from Banu Qurayzah, came to him. He bought me from him and took me to Medina. By Allah, it was only when I saw it that I recognized it by my companion's description. I stayed there. Allah sent His Messenger. He stayed in Mecca as long as he stayed. I did not hear any mention of him due to what I was in of the occupation of slavery. Then he migrated to Medina. By Allah, I was in the top of a palm tree belonging to my master, working in it, and my master was sitting. A cousin of his came and stood by him. He said: ""Woe to Banu Qaylah! By Allah, they are now gathered at Quba' around a man who has come to them from Mecca today claiming he is a Prophet.""

When I heard it, a shudder seized me until I thought I would fall on my master. I climbed down from the palm tree and began saying to his cousin: ""What is that? What do you say? What do you say?"" My master became angry and punched me a severe blow, saying: ""What have you to do with this? Get on with your work!"" I said: ""Nothing. I only wanted to ascertain what he said.""

I had something I had collected. When evening came, I took it and went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Quba'. I entered upon him and said: ""It has reached me that you are a righteous man, and with you are companions who are strangers in need. This is something I had for charity, and I saw you more deserving of it than others."" I brought it near to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his companions: ""Eat,"" and he withheld his hand and did not eat. I said to myself: ""This is one.""

Then I turned away from him. I collected something else, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ moved to Medina. Then I came with it and said: ""I saw you do not eat charity, and this is a gift with which I have honored you."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate from it and commanded his companions, and they ate with him. I said to myself: ""These are two.""

Then I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was at Baqi' al-Gharqad. He had followed a funeral of one of his companions. He had two cloaks on and was sitting among his companions. I greeted him, then I moved around to look at his back to see if I could see the Seal my companion had described to me. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw me moving around him, he knew I was ascertaining something described to me. He threw his cloak off his back. I looked at the Seal and recognized it. I threw myself upon him, kissing it and weeping. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: ""Turn around."" So I turned around. I narrated my story to him as I have narrated it to you, O Ibn Abbas.

The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was pleased that his companions should hear that. Then slavery occupied Salman until he missed Badr and Uhud with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: ""Make a contract (for manumission), O Salman."" So I contracted with my master for three hundred date palms to be planted for him by the poor (or: by the Furay' - a specific measure/method), and forty Uqiyahs (of silver).

The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Help your brother."" So they helped me with the palm shoots: a man with thirty shoots, a man with twenty, a man with fifteen, a man with ten—each man according to what he had—until three hundred shoots were gathered for me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: ""Go, O Salman! Dig holes for them. When you are finished, come to me so that I may plant them with my own hands."" I dug holes for them, and my companions helped me until I finished. I came to him and informed him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out with me to them. We brought the shoots near to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ planted them with his hand. By Him in Whose hand is the soul of Salman, not a single shoot died. I fulfilled the palms, but the money (silver) remained due from me.

The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a piece of gold the size of a hen's egg from some expedition. He said: ""What did the Persian manumitted slave do?"" I was summoned for him. He said: ""Take this and pay off what is upon you, O Salman."" I said: ""Where does this fall, O Messenger of Allah, compared to what is upon me?"" He said: ""Take it, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic,"
