"299","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 299 Arabic Hadees: 712"
"300","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: A Jew entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: ""As-samu 'alayka, O Muhammad!"" (Death be upon you). The Prophet ﷺ replied: ""Wa 'alayk"" (And upon you). I intended to speak, but I perceived the Prophet's ﷺ dislike for that, so I remained silent. Then another entered and said: ""As-samu 'alayka."" He said: "" 'Alayk"" (Upon you). I intended to speak, but I perceived the Prophet's ﷺ dislike for that. Then a third entered and said: ""As-samu 'alayka."" I could not restrain myself until I said: ""And upon you be death, and the wrath of Allah and His curse, O brothers of apes and pigs! Do you greet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with that which Allah has not greeted him with?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Indeed, Allah does not love obscenity nor the practice of it."" They said: ""A word, so we returned it upon them. Indeed, the Jews are a people of envy, and they do not envy us over anything as they envy us over the Salam (greeting of peace) and over the Amin."""
