"309","A man followed us who was not with us when we were invited; if you permit him, he may enter. This is reported from the hadith of Abu Mas'ud al-Badri and Jabir ibn Abdullah. This is the wording of Abu Mas'ud al-Badri's hadith: He said: A man named Abu Shu'ayb came to his servant, a butcher, and said: ""Prepare food for me sufficient for five, for I saw hunger in the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)."" So he prepared food, then sent word to the Prophet (peace be upon him) inviting him and his companions who were with him. When the Prophet (peace be upon him) stood up, a man who had not been with them when they were invited followed them. When the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) reached the door, he said to the owner of the house... and he mentioned it. He said: ""We have permitted him, so let him enter."""
