"352","On the authority of Abū Dharr, who said, marfūʿan: ""Upon every person, on every day the sun rises, there is a charity due from him upon himself."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! From where do I give charity when we possess no wealth?"" He said: ""For indeed among the doors of charity are: the takbīr, the tasbīḥ, the taḥmīd, the tahlīl, the istighfār, enjoining good, forbidding evil, removing the thorn from the path of people, the bone, and the stone, guiding the blind, making the deaf and the mute understand until they comprehend, guiding the seeker to a need he has whose location you know, striving with the strength of your legs to the distressed one crying for help, and supporting the weak with the strength of your arms. All of that is from the doors of charity from you upon yourself. And for you in your sexual intercourse with your wife is a reward."" Abū Dharr said: ""How can there be a reward for me in my desire?"" He said: ""Do you see, if you had a child, then he reached maturity and you hoped for his goodness, then he died, would you seek reward for him?"" I said: ""Yes."" He said: ""So you created him?"" He said: ""Rather, Allah created him."" He said: ""So you guided him?"" He said: ""Rather, Allah guided him."" He said: ""So you provided for him?"" He said: ""Rather, Allah was the One providing for him."" He said: ""Likewise, so place it in its lawful place and avoid its unlawful place; for if Allah wills, He will give it life, and if He wills, He will cause it to die, and for you is a reward."""
